    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4086" root="تم" body-key="t">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تِمٌّ</span></b>  an inf. n. of 1, in the first of the senses
explained above. (M, K.) See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَامٌ</span>, in five
places: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَامٌّ</span>, in three places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>i. q.</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَأْسٌ</span> [app. here meaning <i>A kind of hoe</i>]: (IAar,
T, K:) or <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِسْحَاةٌ</span> [<i>a spade,</i> or <i>a shovel</i>]:
(K:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تِمَمَةٌ</span> (IAar, T,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تِمَمٌ</span>. (So in the
TA.)

